# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: cador-entget-subclass-layout-and-record-pointers -- after the header, cador's entget layout and its table records still differ from the vendors
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: cador-entget-owner-and-header-layout
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-22

* Symptom

Measured with the entget-pointers probe, section 10 (MR !471, BricsCAD V26
macOS job 17397066992), against cador 2.3.30, whose HEADER (-1 0 5 [102]
330) now matches:

| object                        | BricsCAD V26                                        | cador 2.3.30                |
|-------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------|
| LINE                          | -1 0 5 330 100 67 410 8 100 10 11 210               | -1 0 5 330 8 10 11 100 100  |
| TEXT                          | ... 100 67 410 8 100 10 40 1 50 41 51 7 71 72 11 210 100 73 | ... 8 10 40 1 100 100 100 |
| layer 0 record (tblobjname)   | -1 0 5 330 100 100 2 70 62 6 290 370 390 347        | -1 0 2                      |
| block record (tblobjname)     | -1 0 5 330 100 67 8 100 2 70 71 10 3 1 -2 (a BLOCK) | -1 0 2 70 10 -2             |
| (tblobjname "BLOCK" "*Model_Space") | 0 = "BLOCK" (the BLOCK entity)                | 0 = "BLOCK_RECORD"          |
| (entget (namedobjdict))       | 16 default 3/350 entries (ACAD_* / Bricsys)         | none                        |

1. Subclass markers: cador appends the (100 . "AcDbEntity") / (100 .
   "AcDb<Type>") markers at the END; the vendors put AcDbEntity right after
   the owner, with the common groups (67, 410, 8) under it, and the
   type's marker before its own groups (entmake-duplicates-subclass-markers
   is the related write-side ticket).
2. Defaults the vendors list: 67 (space), 410 (layout name), 210
   (extrusion), and per type (TEXT 50 41 51 7 71 72 73 ...).
3. Table records have no 5 / 330 (owner TABLE) / 100 markers, nor the
   layer's 390 (ACDBPLACEHOLDER) and 347 (MATERIAL) pointers; their ids are
   gensyms (TBL-n), not handles, so handent cannot reach them.
4. tblobjname "BLOCK" returns the BLOCK *entity* on BricsCAD (its 330 is
   the BLOCK_RECORD a LINE's 330 names -- "eq NIL" in the probe), the
   BLOCK_RECORD on cador.
5. The named-object dictionary of a fresh drawing has the vendors'
   default entries (ACAD_GROUP, ACAD_LAYOUT, ...).

AutoCAD 2022: to measure with the same section (Windows runners); its
2026-10-08 data put a free XRECORD's 330 BEFORE its 5.

* To do

Measure AutoCAD, then take the items one at a time (each changes what
entget shows, so each needs the entmake / entmod round trip kept
storing nothing synthesized -- see %DROP-VIEW-ONLY-GROUPS).

* AutoCAD 2022 measured (2026-10-24, probe:entget-pointers:autocad:windows, job 17436788251)

Section 10 on AutoCAD, after its own header (-1 0 330 5):
  LINE    100 67 410 8 100 10 11 210
  CIRCLE  100 67 410 8 100 10 40 210
  TEXT    100 67 410 8 100 10 40 1 50 41 51 7 71 72 11 210 100 73
  INSERT  100 67 410 8 100 2 10 41 42 43 50 70 71 44 45 210
  layer 0 record   -1 0 5 102 360 102 330 100 100 2 70 62 6 290 370 390 347 348
  block record     -1 0 330 5 100 67 8 100 70 10 -2 2 1   (a BLOCK)
  tblobjname "BLOCK" "*Model_Space"  ... 0 = "BLOCK"; the LINE's 330 is the
                   BLOCK_RECORD ("eq NIL", as on BricsCAD)
  namedobjdict     -1 0 330 5 100 280 281 then 3/350 pairs (17 entries)
The body is the SAME on both products; only the header differs (already
modelled).

* Items 1 and 2 done (clautolisp 2.3.51)

%VENDOR-BODY-ORDER (cador entity-api) lays the VIEW out as measured:
(100 . "AcDbEntity"), the common groups (*ENTGET-COMMON-CODES*: 67 410 8 6 62
...), then each subclass marker and its groups (*ENTGET-TYPE-LAYOUT*:
measured for LINE, CIRCLE, TEXT, INSERT; the DXF reference's split for ARC,
POINT, ATTRIB, ATTDEF), with the defaults shown when absent for the measured
types (*ENTGET-TYPE-DEFAULTS*: 210 (0 0 1); TEXT 50 0, 41 1, 51 0, 7
"Standard", 71 0, 72 0, 11 (0 0 0), 73 0; INSERT 41 42 43 1, 50 0, 70 71 0,
44 45 0); 67 is 0 / 1 for a model / paper space entity, 410 "Model" for a
model space one. Only the view changes. Round trips checked: (entmakex (cdr
(entget e))) and (entmod (entget e)) twice give the same layout, with no
marker twice. Test ENTGET-BODY-LAYOUT-FOLLOWS-THE-VENDORS (cador).

* Remaining

3. Table records: 5 / 330 (owner TABLE) / 100 markers, the layer's 360 / 390
   (ACDBPLACEHOLDER) / 347 (MATERIAL) / 348 pointers, handles instead of
   TBL-n gensyms (handent).
4. tblobjname "BLOCK" answers the BLOCK entity (its 330 the BLOCK_RECORD).
5. The named-object dictionary of a fresh drawing: the vendors' default
   entries (17 on AutoCAD 2022, 16 on BricsCAD V26).

* Items 3 to 5 done (clautolisp 2.3.52)

Measured first: entget-pointers section 11 (MR !484; AutoCAD 2022 job
17439813490, BricsCAD V25 Windows 17439813491, V26 macOS 17439813492 -- the
two BricsCADs agree):
  NOD           AutoCAD 15 entries (ACAD_CIP_PREVIOUS_PRODUCT_INFO XRECORD,
                ACAD_COLOR, ...); BricsCAD 16 (ACAD_IMAGE_DICT, ACAD_IMAGE_VARS
                RASTERVARIABLES, ACAD_RENDER_ACTIVE_SETTINGS, no ACAD_COLOR);
                both ACAD_PLOTSTYLENAME ACDBDICTIONARYWDFLT, plus PRORD<n> /
                PRPTR<n> XRECORDs
  layer's 330   the LAYER TABLE: BricsCAD -1 0 2 5 100 70, AutoCAD -1 0 2 5
                {ACAD_XDICTIONARY 360} 330 100 70; 70 = 1
  layer's 390   ACDBPLACEHOLDER (-1 0 5 102 330 102 330)
  layer's 347   MATERIAL "Global"
  handent       of layer 0's handle ("10" on both) is EQ to tblobjname's
  BLOCK's 330   the BLOCK_RECORD: AutoCAD -1 0 330 5 100 100 2 360 340 {BLKREFS}
                70 280 281, BricsCAD -1 0 5 330 100 100 2 360 {BLKREFS} 70 280
                281; entnext of the BLOCK is the block's LINE

Done:
3. ADD-TABLE-RECORD / ENSURE-RECORD-HANDLE (drawing): a record's id is its
   hex handle (the file's 5, else the replaced record's, else allocated), in
   the entities' handle space; the DXF writer emits it. HANDENT reaches
   records. The record's entget (%TABLE-RECORD-ENTGET-VIEW): 0 5 330 (its
   TABLE, or the 330 it was read with) in each product's order, the two
   markers, then *RECORD-LAYOUTS* (layer 2 70 62 6 290 370 390 347 with the
   defaults; block record 2 70 280 281). The TABLE objects are views with
   AutoCAD's fixed handles (1 BLOCK_RECORD, 2 LAYER, 3 STYLE, 5 LTYPE, ...).
4. (tblobjname "BLOCK" n) is the BLOCK entity (%BLOCK-ENTITY-VIEW, each
   product's layout), with its own handle (the header's 5, or one assigned);
   its 330 is the BLOCK_RECORD every entity's 330 names; ENTMAKEX of a BLOCK
   returns it; entnext from it walks the block.
5. %ENSURE-ROOT-DICTIONARY (cador): a fresh NOD gets the product's default
   entries (BricsCAD dialects BricsCAD's, others AutoCAD's); Normal and
   ByBlock / ByLayer / Global made, DBMOD untouched. entnext walks graphical
   entities only (it returned the NOD before). The new object types are
   registered non-graphical families.

Tests: ENTGET-TABLE-RECORDS-BLOCKS-AND-NOD-FOLLOW-THE-VENDORS (cador, both
products); the handle-pinned tests now follow the records taking the first
handles. A template drawing with the defaults still saves as DWG with its
entities (checked locally). What is not modelled (other dictionaries'
contents, MATERIAL bodies, extension dictionaries, OBJECTS-section writing)
is issues/open/deferred-nod-default-contents.issue.
